It's here! It's here! It's here!

69
00:04:29,123 --> 00:04:30,463
Come this way!

70
00:04:30,463 --> 00:04:32,796
[Princes]

71
00:04:32,796 --> 00:04:35,697
[The game losers are]

72
00:04:35,697 --> 00:04:37,797
[Real paupers]
It's so cold.

73
00:04:37,797 --> 00:04:39,830
I plan to be a prince, all the way.

74
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:42,530
[Want to be a prince?]

75
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:44,263
[A fierce competition is a given]
No way, this isn't right!

76
00:04:44,263 --> 00:04:45,830
Why!

77
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:47,730
[Run, run, run, run, run, run, run!]
Ugh, I'm seriously so tired!

78
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:50,796
[Gestures full of brotherly love]

79
00:04:50,796 --> 00:04:54,663
[Everyone takes the games very seriously]

80
00:04:54,663 --> 00:04:57,166
[Sometimes you gotta
show your cute, playful side]

81
00:04:57,166 --> 00:04:58,996
I… My run fast.

82
00:04:58,996 --> 00:05:00,730
Oh my god. Th-ro-ro-ro-ro.

83
00:05:00,730 --> 00:05:02,963
One more time. Pl... please…

84
00:05:02,963 --> 00:05:05,496
[Why are they taking it this far…?]
So, this is what success tastes like.

85
00:05:05,496 --> 00:05:07,951
[Princes get a feast fit for royalty]

86
00:05:07,951 --> 00:05:10,963
[Luxurious accommodations provided]
Wow, this place is amazing!

87
00:05:10,963 --> 00:05:13,397
[Paupers... fend for themselves]
I wanna go home…

88
00:05:13,397 --> 00:05:14,657
[By the way, in Egypt]
It's freezing cold!

89
00:05:14,657 --> 00:05:17,430
[There's no place to run or hide]

90
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:19,770
[Pauper life is the absolute worst]
It was truly the worst of the worst!

91
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:21,763
[Will it be a high-end luxury trip]
My name is Prince.

92
00:05:21,763 --> 00:05:23,430
[Or a rock-bottom nightmare of a trip?]
Wow, I'm seriously a pauper.

93
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:26,196
[Unfolding all across Egypt]

94
00:05:26,196 --> 00:05:28,763
[A survival trip at opposite extremes]
The first one…! 3 to the side!

95
00:05:28,763 --> 00:05:31,563
I'll finish this in 5 minutes flat! Perfectly.

96
00:05:31,563 --> 00:05:33,530
[Despair all you want]
I am…

97
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:35,296
I am a pauper!!!

98
00:05:35,296 --> 00:05:37,530
[And fail miserably!]

99
00:05:37,530 --> 00:05:39,430
[Only those who let it all go]

100
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,763
[Will become princes...]
Wow, Johnny is just…!

101
00:05:41,763 --> 00:05:43,597
I am… I am a prince!

102
00:05:43,597 --> 00:05:44,996
I'm a prince! Finally!

103
00:05:44,996 --> 00:05:46,563
I am a prince!

104
00:05:46,563 --> 00:05:47,763
Shin Dong, usually…

105
00:05:47,763 --> 00:05:49,563
Are reality shows usually this hard?

106
00:05:49,563 --> 00:05:52,196
[Epic mukbangs are a given!]
This is seriously delicious.

107
00:05:52,196 --> 00:05:55,730
[Friends are made at the market]

108
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,197
[And visiting stunning places, like a travel show]
I feel so overpowered…

109
00:05:57,197 --> 00:05:58,935
- Right?
- This is no joke.

110
00:05:58,935 --> 00:06:01,171
- Why does it feel so unreal here?
- Right?

111
00:06:01,171 --> 00:06:04,816
[Just watching this boosts happiness by 100%]

112
00:06:04,816 --> 00:06:05,976
Nice one!

113
00:06:05,976 --> 00:06:08,445
APT. APT. APT. APT.

114
00:06:08,445 --> 00:06:10,930
[Please enjoy this romantic trip to Egypt with us]

115
00:06:10,930 --> 00:06:12,914
- Why did we come to Egypt?
- I trust the production team.

116
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,451
[They head to their destination]
Right.

117
00:06:14,451 --> 00:06:18,063
But isn't this lineup
of people kind of unusual?

118
00:06:18,063 --> 00:06:21,598
- Of all time! It's a unique mix.
- A totally weird combo.

119
00:06:21,598 --> 00:06:23,586
[The WANGGEOZ lineup is familiar, yet new]
I'm really curious why

120
00:06:23,586 --> 00:06:25,197
they grouped us like this.

121
00:06:25,197 --> 00:06:27,629
- Ji Sung, what year were you born?
- I was born in 2002.

122
00:06:27,629 --> 00:06:30,029
Wow, that's like
a 30-year gap with Lee Teuk.

123
00:06:30,029 --> 00:06:31,096
No!

124
00:06:31,096 --> 00:06:34,296
We're exactly 20 years apart.
I started college in 2002.

125
00:06:34,296 --> 00:06:36,630
[Wow…ancestor-status]
Wow…

126
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:39,430
- You're a World Cup baby.
- That's right.

127
00:06:39,430 --> 00:06:40,829
You must hear
that all the time, right?

128
00:06:40,829 --> 00:06:41,818
[What 2002 babies hear on repeat]
Yeah, all the time.

129
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:43,663
- Right? You hear it all the time?
- I hear it all the time.

130
00:06:43,663 --> 00:06:46,029
Then, who's the youngest here?
Ji Sung?

131
00:06:46,029 --> 00:06:47,438
- I think it's me.
- Were you born in 2000?

132
00:06:47,438 --> 00:06:49,561
- I was born in 2002.
- 2002, and who's next?

133
00:06:49,561 --> 00:06:51,197
[Yo Han, born in 1999]
I was born in 1999.

134
00:06:51,197 --> 00:06:52,763
Yo Han, that's your birth name, right?

135
00:06:52,763 --> 00:06:54,696
Yes, it's my birth name.

136
00:06:55,263 --> 00:06:57,227
[DAWN, born in 1994]
I was born in 1994.

137
00:06:57,227 --> 00:06:59,382
[Johnny, born in 1995]
Johnny was born in 1995.

138
00:06:59,382 --> 00:07:00,540
The number suddenly shoots up.

139
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:01,798
[Jump! Shin Dong, born in 1985]
I was born in 1985.

140
00:07:01,798 --> 00:07:03,336
It just suddenly shot up.

141
00:07:03,336 --> 00:07:05,402
[Soaring like a semiconductor stock chart]
1985. Lee Teuk was 1983.

142
00:07:05,402 --> 00:07:07,569
Oh, I'm so old!
I don't wanna be here!

143
00:07:08,263 --> 00:07:09,796
Is this like an elimination show or something?

144
00:07:09,796 --> 00:07:12,030
[Lee Teuk 44 - Shin Dong 42 -
DAWN 33 -Johnny 32 -Yo Han 28 -Ji Sung 25]

145
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:13,430
Hey, but what's with your eyes?

146
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:14,763
Oh, this…

147
00:07:14,763 --> 00:07:16,130
[Ji Sung's eyes are red]
Because you're tired?

148
00:07:16,130 --> 00:07:17,363
I cried so much
that the blood vessels popped.

149
00:07:17,363 --> 00:07:19,030
- You cried so much? Yeah.
- Why?

150
00:07:19,030 --> 00:07:20,130
Because you didn't wanna come to Egypt?

151
00:07:20,130 --> 00:07:21,896
[Ji Sung's on a NCT DREAM tour]
After the concert…

152
00:07:21,896 --> 00:07:25,597
[He cried during the encore stage]
Oh, then! That's understandable.

153
00:07:25,597 --> 00:07:27,524
I found out for the first time.

154
00:07:27,524 --> 00:07:29,149
[Thankfully, he says it doesn't hurt]
So the vessels burst from crying too much?

155
00:07:29,149 --> 00:07:31,730
I just found out too.

156
00:07:31,730 --> 00:07:34,033
It's everyone's
first time in Egypt, right?

157
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:35,030
- Totally my first time.
- That's right.

158
00:07:35,030 --> 00:07:37,367
When I heard
we were going to Egypt,

159
00:07:37,367 --> 00:07:38,849
[Interest #1: The Pyramids]
I thought it'd be worth it

160
00:07:38,849 --> 00:07:40,550
to see the pyramids once.

161
00:07:40,550 --> 00:07:41,775
[Interest #2: Soccer star Mohamed Salah]
Salah.

162
00:07:41,775 --> 00:07:43,473
- Salah, the soccer player.
- Salah.

163
00:07:43,473 --> 00:07:44,509
Right, Salah.

164
00:07:44,509 --> 00:07:46,009
[Salah, a national hero hailed as the King of Egypt]
Is there a famous soccer player?

165
00:07:46,009 --> 00:07:47,040
Yeah.

166
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,130
[Interest #3: Desserts]
I heard Egyptian desserts are famous.

167
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:50,197
- Desserts?
- Desserts?

168
00:07:50,197 --> 00:07:52,163
[Everyone's interested in different things]
Desserts.

169
00:07:52,163 --> 00:07:54,985
- Koshari.
- What's that?

170
00:07:54,985 --> 00:07:56,277
For Egypt, isn't it ROSÉ?

171
00:07:56,277 --> 00:07:58,896
Egypt, Egypt…

172
00:07:58,896 --> 00:08:00,991
[Doubting their own ears]

173
00:08:00,991 --> 00:08:02,225
[Sorry]

174
00:08:02,225 --> 00:08:04,993
[Oh my god...]

175
00:08:04,993 --> 00:08:07,163
[Brace yourself]
He's gonna keep throwing out things like this.

176
00:08:07,163 --> 00:08:08,996
[Holding back, since he's the oldest]
You gotta get used to it, okay?

177
00:08:08,996 --> 00:08:11,863
- You have to get used to it. Sorry.
- But even now, the pyramids…

178
00:08:11,863 --> 00:08:13,031
[The unresolved mystery
of how the pyramids were built]

179
00:08:13,031 --> 00:08:16,763
- Isn't how they were built a mystery?
- Some stuff has come up…

180
00:08:16,763 --> 00:08:18,463
- They're all just theories, though.
- Right?

181
00:08:18,463 --> 00:08:20,530
- An enigma?
- It's all speculation. Theories.

182
00:08:20,530 --> 00:08:23,396
Like, some say they
built them as long staircases.

183
00:08:23,396 --> 00:08:25,596
Someone mentioned
it was a city submerged underwater…

184
00:08:25,596 --> 00:08:27,163
That was me.

185
00:08:27,163 --> 00:08:28,796
So they built it underwater?

186
00:08:28,796 --> 00:08:31,196
So, "It used to be
a city submerged underwater."

187
00:08:31,196 --> 00:08:33,757
I always thought giants built them.

188
00:08:33,757 --> 00:08:35,125
Giants?

189
00:08:35,125 --> 00:08:36,560
Seo Jang Hoon?

190
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:37,827
[He is a giant]
You mean Jang Hoon?

191
00:08:37,827 --> 00:08:38,863
Did Jang Hoon build it?

192
00:08:38,863 --> 00:08:40,896
How giant does the giant have to be?
- Like Choi Hong Man?

193
00:08:40,896 --> 00:08:42,097
[Totally his vibe]
Seo… Jang Hoon…

194
00:08:42,097 --> 00:08:44,463
[Determined]
Didn't they find giant skeletons or something?

195
00:08:44,463 --> 00:08:46,863
It seems like DAWN
watches a lot of fake news.

196
00:08:46,863 --> 00:08:48,231
[Hehe]
Try looking it up.

197
00:08:48,231 --> 00:08:50,006
Where do you get your news?

198
00:08:50,006 --> 00:08:52,672
- But I really saw the photos!
- Really?

199
00:08:52,672 --> 00:08:54,044
[He swears]
Giants...

200
00:08:54,044 --> 00:08:56,663
Please search for
"Pyramids, giants."

201
00:08:56,663 --> 00:08:59,496
[Shin Dong] How come the buildings
all look the same, no matter how far we go?

202
00:08:59,496 --> 00:09:01,196
They look really interesting.

203
00:09:01,196 --> 00:09:03,162
- Even the colors are all the same.
- Yeah.

204
00:09:03,162 --> 00:09:05,329
[Observation mode]
The colors are all kind of the same.

205
00:09:05,329 --> 00:09:07,463
- Did they match the tone on purpose?
- Are they building it with the dirt here?

206
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:08,896
[Because of the desert sandstorms,
most buildings in Cairo are beige-toned]

207
00:09:08,896 --> 00:09:11,829
Everything's beige,
because there's a lot of sand.

208
00:09:12,497 --> 00:09:14,363
- That's a redevelopment zone over there.
- Huh? What's this place?

209
00:09:14,363 --> 00:09:17,196
Is this some kind of historic site?

210
00:09:17,196 --> 00:09:19,096
- Oh, it's being redeveloped?
- A redevelopment zone, right?

211
00:09:19,096 --> 00:09:20,296
Oh, it's a redevelopment zone?

212
00:09:20,296 --> 00:09:23,362
- Isn't that the redevelopment area over there?
- Oh, this is the redevelopment zone?

213
00:09:23,362 --> 00:09:25,162
Hey! Then you should've bought land!

214
00:09:25,162 --> 00:09:27,796
- You should've bought it all!
- Did they clear everything out?

215
00:09:27,796 --> 00:09:30,363
This must be a movie set.

216
00:09:30,363 --> 00:09:32,429
Is "Arabian Nights" from Egypt?

217
00:09:32,429 --> 00:09:35,196
[Not sure why, but everyone starts laughing]

218
00:09:35,196 --> 00:09:36,233
[Suddenly, his host instincts kick in]

219
00:09:36,233 --> 00:09:39,029
Honestly, if we talk about Egypt
right now, we don't really know much.

220
00:09:39,029 --> 00:09:41,128
[Listening]
So as we travel,

221
00:09:41,128 --> 00:09:43,329
we'll get to know and learn
more about Egypt.

222
00:09:43,329 --> 00:09:46,929
And we'll share about Egypt
with everyone watching this!

223
00:09:46,929 --> 00:09:49,306
- That's right.
- Oh, it's that kind of broadcast?

224
00:09:49,306 --> 00:09:50,372
[Lee Teuk jumped to his own conclusion]
It's not?

225
00:09:50,372 --> 00:09:51,734
I've only done shows like that.

226
00:09:51,734 --> 00:09:53,363
Lee Teuk, the script… Where is your script?

227
00:09:53,363 --> 00:09:54,462
I've only done that kind of show.

228
00:09:54,462 --> 00:09:57,240
[Can't help but keep laughing for some reason]
Isn't this an Egypt product placement?

229
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,463
It's like…

230
00:09:58,463 --> 00:09:59,829
But where are we headed?

231
00:09:59,829 --> 00:10:00,996
Yeah, where are we going?

232
00:10:00,996 --> 00:10:03,463
We know nothing.

233
00:10:03,463 --> 00:10:04,763
Oh! Over there!

234
00:10:04,763 --> 00:10:07,329
- Oh! Over there!
- Where?

235
00:10:07,329 --> 00:10:08,618
- Over there!
- Oh, wow!

236
00:10:08,618 --> 00:10:10,048
- Oh, the pyramids!
- There!

237
00:10:10,048 --> 00:10:10,983
On the right?

238
00:10:10,983 --> 00:10:12,196
- Over there!
- Whoa, amazing!

239
00:10:12,196 --> 00:10:13,863
[Pyramids in sight!]

240
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:14,863
What? That…

241
00:10:14,863 --> 00:10:16,563
[Johnny wants to see the pyramids too...]
That's how big it is? On the right?

242
00:10:16,563 --> 00:10:18,296
- Over there!
- Whoa, amazing!

243
00:10:18,296 --> 00:10:20,164
[Kept mirroring Shin Dong's line of movement]

244
00:10:20,164 --> 00:10:23,363
- That's how big it is?
- The pyramid! The pyramid!

245
00:10:23,363 --> 00:10:26,303
[This is seriously surreal!]
Wow!

246
00:10:26,303 --> 00:10:27,559
- Wow, I just got chills.
- It's really huge.

247
00:10:27,559 --> 00:10:28,797
Oh, I'm suddenly wide awake!

248
00:10:28,797 --> 00:10:30,630
[Can't believe I'm seeing such a grand
and huge monument with my own eyes…!]

249
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:32,496
It's really huge.

250
00:10:32,943 --> 00:10:34,511
Right next to the city.

251
00:10:34,511 --> 00:10:36,903
[The pyramids are
right next to the city!]

252
00:10:36,903 --> 00:10:38,515
Wow…

253
00:10:38,515 --> 00:10:41,030
I thought
we'd see them on the last day.

254
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:43,596
But we saw them from the start,
so it was so surprising and amazing.

255
00:10:43,596 --> 00:10:46,096
[For his personal collection]

256
00:10:46,096 --> 00:10:48,663
When Lee Teuk said,
"Look over there," I looked to the right.

257
00:10:48,663 --> 00:10:51,430
And the pyramids were huge!

258
00:10:51,430 --> 00:10:52,730
Wow, they're that big?!

259
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:54,564
I honestly got goosebumps.

260
00:10:54,564 --> 00:10:56,396
I was like "Wow".

261
00:10:56,396 --> 00:10:58,130
It's seriously massive!

262
00:10:58,130 --> 00:10:59,730
Oh, but, seeing it up close like this,

263
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:04,107
[Finally get why it's a wonder of the world]
I understand why people wonder about it.

264
00:11:04,107 --> 00:11:06,042
Right? How did they even build that?

265
00:11:06,042 --> 00:11:08,277
The height is…

266
00:11:08,277 --> 00:11:11,314
- If we go close by, it'll be super high.
- They built a whole mountain.

267
00:11:11,314 --> 00:11:13,162
[For some reason, it feels like a reward]
It's really tall.

268
00:11:13,162 --> 00:11:15,496
Just how tall is it, though?
Is it as tall as Namsan Tower?

269
00:11:15,496 --> 00:11:16,796
Wow! Oh, there are two!

270
00:11:16,796 --> 00:11:18,563
- No, there's more.
- There are three of them.

271
00:11:18,563 --> 00:11:21,696
- Oh, there's a tiny one over there, too.
- There are so many.

272
00:11:21,696 --> 00:11:23,497
[Whispering]
This is seriously amazing.

273
00:11:23,497 --> 00:11:25,263
Isn't it one of the Three Wonders of the World?

274
00:11:25,263 --> 00:11:26,330
Isn't it the Seven Wonders of the World?

275
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:27,463
- Seven…
- Oh, it's seven?

276
00:11:27,463 --> 00:11:28,831
Wow, that list keeps growing

277
00:11:28,831 --> 00:11:31,996
[LOL]
The list keeps growing…!

278
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:37,272
Oh, we're getting closer!

279
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,308
[Everything's amazing]
Those camels are really tall.

280
00:11:39,308 --> 00:11:42,312
Wait, can the bus
actually get this close?

281
00:11:42,312 --> 00:11:43,945
Wow.

282
00:11:44,730 --> 00:11:46,336
We're literally right beside it!

283
00:11:46,336 --> 00:11:49,736
[Getting closer to the pyramids]

284
00:11:50,263 --> 00:11:53,930
[Pure wonder]

285
00:11:53,930 --> 00:11:56,395
Does it feel like we're really in Egypt now?
Johnny, what do you think?

286
00:11:56,395 --> 00:11:57,129
It feels like we're here!

287
00:11:57,129 --> 00:12:00,224
- It feels like we are?
- Yes.

288
00:12:00,931 --> 00:12:03,767
[The more you look, the more in awe you are]
Everyone, look to your right.

289
00:12:03,767 --> 00:12:04,634
It's the pyramids.

290
00:12:04,634 --> 00:12:07,037
- Everyone, we're in Egypt right now.
- Wait a sec.

291
00:12:07,037 --> 00:12:08,738
This looks like Cairo,
but it's not actually Cairo.

292
00:12:08,738 --> 00:12:13,730
[This is the view just from the bus]
It's Giza, Giza, Giza.

293
00:12:13,730 --> 00:12:15,396
Look to the left, there's a café.

294
00:12:15,396 --> 00:12:20,029
[A shot of the pyramids by Ji Sung]

295
00:12:20,029 --> 00:12:23,998
They built this 4,600 years ago?

296
00:12:24,963 --> 00:12:26,230
Whoa, pyramids!

297
00:12:26,230 --> 00:12:29,196
Is the café in front
of the pyramids different?

298
00:12:29,196 --> 00:12:30,796
Let's check it out.

299
00:12:32,963 --> 00:12:35,864
[First meetup spot]
[A café with a pyramid view]

300
00:12:35,864 --> 00:12:37,430
[Getting off with excitement]
Let's go!

301
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:38,868
- Wow!
- Wow!

302
00:12:38,868 --> 00:12:41,237
I think it feels hotter
next to the pyramids.

303
00:12:41,237 --> 00:12:42,363
What's this?

304
00:12:42,363 --> 00:12:44,930
Wow!

305
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:48,696
- How many floors do you think that is?
- So fascinating.

306
00:12:48,696 --> 00:12:50,963
The six of us look cool,
all dressed up and walking over.

307
00:12:50,963 --> 00:12:52,363
It kinda feels like we're kings.

308
00:12:52,363 --> 00:12:54,052
[Our WANGGEOZ makes us proud,
no matter where they go]

309
00:12:54,052 --> 00:12:58,321
"The Pyramids of Giza".

310
00:12:58,321 --> 00:13:04,661
It feels so surreal that
the pyramids are actually right there.

311
00:13:05,063 --> 00:13:11,889
[The Great Pyramid of Khufu
stands tall amidst Giza's sandy winds]

312
00:13:11,889 --> 00:13:14,006
[Beneath the blazing desert sun]

313
00:13:14,006 --> 00:13:16,730
[The triangular giants that have
braved sandstorms for thousands of years]

314
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:18,263
[The three pyramids of the Giza Plateau]

315
00:13:18,263 --> 00:13:20,163
[The tombs of King Khufu,
King Khafre, and King Menkaure]

316
00:13:20,163 --> 00:13:22,964
[One can feel the mighty legacy
of a dynasty dreaming of eternity]

317
00:13:22,964 --> 00:13:26,263
[The Sphinx, the guardian of the pyramids]

318
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:31,062
[A massive statue carved
from a whole mountain rock]

319
00:13:32,496 --> 00:13:36,198
[The grandeur of the Great Sphinx]

320
00:13:36,198 --> 00:13:40,498
[In the place where myths breathe,
"ALL or NOTHING" begins its first journey]

321
00:13:40,498 --> 00:13:41,763
What's up with him?

322
00:13:41,763 --> 00:13:43,396
[Everyone, let's snap
some memories before we go]

323
00:13:43,396 --> 00:13:44,500
What's he doing?

324
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:46,970
[Take a photo of Johnny]
You can take a photo of me.

325
00:13:46,970 --> 00:13:48,471
Lee Teuk, come here.
Let's take a photo together.

326
00:13:48,471 --> 00:13:49,771
Alright.

327
00:13:50,963 --> 00:13:53,196
[Shin Dong and Lee Teuk]
Oh, it came out great!

328
00:13:53,196 --> 00:13:55,363
[Can't resist a selfie
in front of the pyramids]

329
00:13:55,363 --> 00:13:57,362
[The pyramid's right here with Ji Sung]

330
00:13:57,362 --> 00:14:02,256
[Not taking a picture of this
would be a crime]

331
00:14:04,096 --> 00:14:08,530
[Shining even brighter
in front of the pyramids]

332
00:14:08,530 --> 00:14:13,056
[The handsome faces of
our soon-to-be princes and paupers]

333
00:14:13,056 --> 00:14:16,430
[Looking sharp, Johnny]

334
00:14:16,430 --> 00:14:21,995
[Let's soak up the good energy here
in the land of living myths]

335
00:14:21,995 --> 00:14:24,348
[We are "ALL or NOTHING"]

336
00:14:24,348 --> 00:14:26,396
Don't you think
the sun is really strong in Egypt?

337
00:14:26,396 --> 00:14:28,396
[Egypt, where the desert sun blazes down]
It's super strong, it's crazy.

338
00:14:28,396 --> 00:14:31,063
I heard using sunscreen
protects your skin really well.

339
00:14:31,063 --> 00:14:33,349
But I hate that sticky feeling.

340
00:14:33,349 --> 00:14:37,087
It's super light, and keeps your skin hydrated.

341
00:14:37,087 --> 00:14:38,220
It's really light.

342
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:41,699
[Sunscreen is a must during this Egypt trip!]
It comes out like water.

343
00:14:41,699 --> 00:14:43,663
So light and moisturizing!

344
00:14:43,663 --> 00:14:45,128
It's so nice!

345
00:14:45,128 --> 00:14:46,730
[His English pronunciation boosts credibility]
It feels light.

346
00:14:46,730 --> 00:14:48,096
Your English pronunciation is great.

347
00:14:48,096 --> 00:14:49,363
How does it feel?

348
00:14:49,363 --> 00:14:52,363
Totally light! Not sticky at all.

349
00:14:52,363 --> 00:14:55,263
Can heavy guys use this?

350
00:14:55,263 --> 00:14:57,463
- Maybe you'll feel lighter.
- Shin Dong, you'll feel lighter!

351
00:14:57,463 --> 00:14:59,096
[Getting lighter]
I feel like I'm getting lighter!

352
00:14:59,096 --> 00:15:01,863
Just holding it makes me feel lighter.

353
00:15:01,863 --> 00:15:04,910
[Johnny's skin is precious]
I should take one.

354
00:15:05,463 --> 00:15:10,031
Alright, everyone. Welcome to Egypt.

355
00:15:10,031 --> 00:15:11,697
But isn't it starting
to really hit you now?

356
00:15:11,697 --> 00:15:13,440
Since we're in front of the pyramids.

357
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:16,497
Honestly, I had a dopamine rush
as soon as I saw the pyramids.

358
00:15:16,497 --> 00:15:17,996
- Yeah, yeah.
- I know, right?

359
00:15:17,996 --> 00:15:19,895
- Here…
- You must be an F-type. Are you an F-type?

360
00:15:19,895 --> 00:15:20,964
[A totally capital T]
I'm a total T-type.

361
00:15:20,964 --> 00:15:22,330
Oh really? Even T-types are moved by this?

362
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:27,563
As you all know,
we're here together for a travel show.

363
00:15:27,563 --> 00:15:31,429
To fully experience this trip,

364
00:15:31,429 --> 00:15:34,697
you just have to enjoy
the missions and the games

365
00:15:34,697 --> 00:15:36,896
that we prepared.

366
00:15:36,896 --> 00:15:38,430
- Nothing's free.
- Oh, so there are missions?

367
00:15:38,430 --> 00:15:39,983
No freebies.

368
00:15:39,983 --> 00:15:42,085
Depending on the results,
as you know,

369
00:15:42,085 --> 00:15:44,888
some will get
to live it up in luxury.

370
00:15:44,888 --> 00:15:46,063
[Some will lose it all on this trip]

371
00:15:46,063 --> 00:15:49,123
And those who lose
will lose absolutely everything.

372
00:15:49,123 --> 00:15:53,496
But if we become paupers,
just how much will we be losing?

373
00:15:53,496 --> 00:15:55,098
[Half worried, half curious]
I'm curious.

374
00:15:55,098 --> 00:15:58,367
In a way, it could be romantic, right?

375
00:15:58,367 --> 00:16:00,803
Do you usually think of those things as romantic?

376
00:16:00,803 --> 00:16:02,363
Like, for example…

377
00:16:02,363 --> 00:16:05,450
[Romanticize mode on]
Pitching tents and sleeping right by the pyramids.

378
00:16:05,450 --> 00:16:06,937
[Isn't that romantic?]
It's not bad to try it once.

379
00:16:06,937 --> 00:16:08,463
Once in a lifetime…!

380
00:16:08,463 --> 00:16:10,563
[Selfless mode at full power]
Then you can do it instead.

381
00:16:10,563 --> 00:16:13,263
[No way]
But, like, we should still play the games.

382
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:15,651
The missions will be done as 3 vs 3,

383
00:16:15,651 --> 00:16:17,196
[Missions will be played as 3 vs 3,
6 vs 0, or a free-for-all]

384
00:16:17,196 --> 00:16:19,296
a free-for-all, or 6 vs 0.

385
00:16:19,296 --> 00:16:21,430
- 6 vs 0.
- What's 6 vs 0?

386
00:16:21,430 --> 00:16:23,296
[6 vs 0: Everyone succeeds or everyone fails]
We team up together and go against the staff.

387
00:16:23,296 --> 00:16:25,630
Honestly, I think
rather than a 3 vs 3 or a 1 vs 1,

388
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,996
a 6 vs 0 will be even more stressful.

389
00:16:27,996 --> 00:16:30,696
- A free-for-all might be better.
- I'm bad at games, so bad.

390
00:16:30,696 --> 00:16:32,163
Then can we decide that ourselves?

391
00:16:32,163 --> 00:16:33,729
Like, will it be 1 vs 1 or 3 vs 3?

392
00:16:33,729 --> 00:16:36,056
Sometimes, we'll assign the teams,

393
00:16:36,056 --> 00:16:38,474
and other times,
we'll give you time to decide on your own.

394
00:16:38,474 --> 00:16:40,142
Then, how about for the first game,

395
00:16:40,142 --> 00:16:41,845
we start together as a group.

396
00:16:41,845 --> 00:16:43,430
Let's go with 6 vs 0.

397
00:16:43,430 --> 00:16:46,016
Oh? We actually have something prepared.

398
00:16:46,016 --> 00:16:47,897
Didn't you say
you'd give us time to decide?

399
00:16:47,897 --> 00:16:50,263
Come on, Lee Teuk.
I thought we were going with 6 vs 0.

400
00:16:50,263 --> 00:16:53,030
I don't vibe well here. I'm gonna leave!

401
00:16:53,030 --> 00:16:56,596
For today, we'll reveal
the first game we've prepared.

402
00:16:56,596 --> 00:16:58,064
- Oh?
- Okay.

403
00:16:58,064 --> 00:16:59,696
I'm getting nervous.

404
00:16:59,696 --> 00:17:02,763
To experience local Egyptian cuisine,

405
00:17:02,763 --> 00:17:04,463
[Pharaoh's Table]
this is the Pharaoh's Table.

406
00:17:04,463 --> 00:17:06,978
- Pharaoh's Table.
- Are we guessing the prices?

407
00:17:09,209 --> 00:17:10,767
Shin Dong's already guessing.

408
00:17:10,767 --> 00:17:12,163
I don't wanna be a pauper!

409
00:17:12,163 --> 00:17:14,663
I've lived that life
since I was a kid!

410
00:17:14,663 --> 00:17:17,993
Sorry, but Shin Dong
and I have that pauper instinct.

411
00:17:17,993 --> 00:17:22,796
Starting in the order of
appetizers, seafood, meats, and dessert,

412
00:17:22,796 --> 00:17:24,329
[A full-course dining mission!]
we've got a full-course meal prepared for you.

413
00:17:24,329 --> 00:17:25,563
- Oh.
- Wow.

414
00:17:25,563 --> 00:17:27,466
- We're gonna eat that?
- That's the mission?

415
00:17:27,466 --> 00:17:29,363
We have to eat everything!
We have to eat everything!

416
00:17:29,363 --> 00:17:32,886
You're not sitting down
in one place for the whole full-course meal.

417
00:17:32,886 --> 00:17:33,746
We have to move around?

418
00:17:33,746 --> 00:17:34,770
[1 Appetizer → Move]
In order of the courses,

419
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:35,865
[2 Seafood → Move]
you'll go around

420
00:17:35,865 --> 00:17:36,899
[3 Meat → Move]
to the restaurants

421
00:17:36,899 --> 00:17:39,369
[4 Dessert → Finish]
we reserved,

422
00:17:39,369 --> 00:17:42,038
and the team that arrives first wins.

423
00:17:42,038 --> 00:17:43,563
[Dopamine's kicking in]
Wow! Hold up!

424
00:17:43,563 --> 00:17:45,909
[We're doing such a huge mission from the start?]
A mission that big already?

425
00:17:45,909 --> 00:17:47,006
Here?

426
00:17:47,006 --> 00:17:47,930
[Pharaoh's Table]

427
00:17:47,930 --> 00:17:50,496
[Hit up selected restaurants
and enjoy Cairo's best food]

428
00:17:50,496 --> 00:17:52,762
[The team that eats first,
up to the last dessert, becomes princes]

429
00:17:52,762 --> 00:17:53,496
[Pharaoh's Table rules]

430
00:17:53,496 --> 00:17:56,229
[Full-course dining order]
[Appetizer → Seafood → Meat → Dessert]

431
00:17:56,229 --> 00:17:57,964
[Each team gets its own transport]

432
00:17:57,964 --> 00:18:03,526
[There are 7 restaurants marked on the map]

433
00:18:03,526 --> 00:18:04,893
Two places for appetizers.

434
00:18:04,893 --> 00:18:06,096
Two places for seafood.

435
00:18:06,096 --> 00:18:08,183
Two places for meat, and lastly,

436
00:18:08,183 --> 00:18:11,433
the final meetup
spot is a dessert café.

437
00:18:11,433 --> 00:18:12,836
[Appetizer]
We're not going to

438
00:18:12,836 --> 00:18:14,537
[Seafood]
reveal where

439
00:18:14,537 --> 00:18:16,430
[Meat]
what restaurant is where just yet.

440
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:18,234
[Seafood A VS Seafood B]

441
00:18:18,234 --> 00:18:20,263
[Listen to a "keyword" and pick
one of the two restaurants for each course!]

442
00:18:20,263 --> 00:18:23,280
[A race where the distance
and menu depend on luck and intuition]

443
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:25,048
So, we don't even know
the names of the restaurants?

444
00:18:25,048 --> 00:18:27,595
No names, no locations.

445
00:18:27,595 --> 00:18:29,229
We're only going
to give you keywords.

446
00:18:29,229 --> 00:18:31,087
[A race based on luck]
[The keyword choices decide everything]

447
00:18:31,087 --> 00:18:34,156
You've seen this
on social media lately, right?

448
00:18:34,156 --> 00:18:37,485
There's a game where
you clear the closest cups first

449
00:18:37,485 --> 00:18:40,163
or clear the farthest cups first.

450
00:18:40,163 --> 00:18:41,664
The person who clears
the farthest cups first always wins.

451
00:18:41,664 --> 00:18:43,678
- That's right.
- Let's go for the farthest spots first.

452
00:18:43,678 --> 00:18:45,730
[So here's the deal,
let's hit up the farthest spots first!]

453
00:18:45,730 --> 00:18:49,306
[Explaining again]
We still don't know which place is where.

454
00:18:49,306 --> 00:18:50,941
Ugh, this game is making my head spin!

455
00:18:50,941 --> 00:18:54,788
We just have to eat well
and finish the chosen courses in order.

456
00:18:54,788 --> 00:18:56,549
[Brainy Shin Dong totally gets it]
Right, since there are two of each,

457
00:18:56,549 --> 00:18:57,916
one team goes this way,
the other team goes that way.

458
00:18:57,916 --> 00:18:59,230
Okay, then first…

459
00:18:59,230 --> 00:19:00,911
Let's talk about

460
00:19:00,911 --> 00:19:03,297
who wants to eat meat
and who wants to eat seafood.

461
00:19:03,297 --> 00:19:04,586
No, that's not it at all.

462
00:19:04,586 --> 00:19:05,625
[Code Red. He doesn't get the rules,
no matter how much we explain them]

463
00:19:05,625 --> 00:19:07,363
- He still doesn't get the game.
- I understand it now.

464
00:19:07,363 --> 00:19:09,725
- You got it?
- Lee Teuk, it's a course meal.

465
00:19:09,725 --> 00:19:12,398
When the game starts,
the two teams can eat three dishes in order.

466
00:19:12,398 --> 00:19:14,197
We're hitting up all the places
for meat, seafood, and appetizers.

467
00:19:14,197 --> 00:19:16,121
- Right, right.
- But there's an A option and a B option for each.

468
00:19:16,121 --> 00:19:17,730
[The star instructor explaining the rules]
We'll choose one. So, we'll keep splitting up.

469
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:18,930
So we decide whether to go to A or B?

470
00:19:18,930 --> 00:19:20,731
For that, we'll choose teams
and head out for each mission.

471
00:19:20,731 --> 00:19:24,430
The staff failed at this game.

472
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:25,596
[Speaking his mind]

473
00:19:25,596 --> 00:19:27,577
That's just how I see it.

474
00:19:27,577 --> 00:19:32,282
But the problem is, we don't know
which is dessert, meat, or seafood here.

475
00:19:32,282 --> 00:19:33,483
Oh!

476
00:19:33,483 --> 00:19:34,596
Because there's a bit
of distance between them.

477
00:19:34,596 --> 00:19:35,796
Oh!!

478
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:39,689
You're all playing
the same game I am, right?

479
00:19:39,689 --> 00:19:41,758
Yo Han is clueless.
Stop pretending you know!

480
00:19:41,758 --> 00:19:44,094
- I have a rough idea.
- Rough? No, you don't have a rough idea.

481
00:19:44,094 --> 00:19:45,128
Then explain it.

482
00:19:45,128 --> 00:19:48,330
So you're saying we start
by clearing the farthest cups first.

483
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:50,097
You and I are pretty much
on the same page right now.

484
00:19:50,097 --> 00:19:51,996
So which cup are we hitting first?

485
00:19:51,996 --> 00:19:53,229
[Let me think...]

486
00:19:53,229 --> 00:19:54,630
Johnny's cup.

487
00:19:54,630 --> 00:19:55,938
[Crinkle]

488
00:19:55,938 --> 00:19:59,663
I was shocked when Yo Han suddenly said
we should clear the farthest cup first.

489
00:19:59,663 --> 00:20:02,896
But why is everyone
struggling to understand the rules?

490
00:20:02,896 --> 00:20:04,491
The Pharaoh's Table will

491
00:20:04,491 --> 00:20:07,530
[The Pharaoh's Table is a 3 vs 3 showdown]
take place as a 3 vs 3 battle.

492
00:20:07,530 --> 00:20:11,730
Since it's the first mission,
we went ahead and picked the teams ourselves.

493
00:20:11,730 --> 00:20:13,630
As long as it's not like this…
Like, 3 vs 3 like this…

494
00:20:13,630 --> 00:20:15,596
- Right now, we're too…
- What? What?

495
00:20:15,596 --> 00:20:19,030
[Reason: All three of them are too gentle]
The three of us are too gentle and soft.

496
00:20:19,030 --> 00:20:20,530
Let's go, let's go!

497
00:20:20,530 --> 00:20:24,164
It's okay, as long as
the SUPER JUNIOR members aren't together.

498
00:20:24,164 --> 00:20:25,898
We'll fight if we're together.

499
00:20:25,898 --> 00:20:29,263
We kept it simple and split the teams

500
00:20:29,263 --> 00:20:30,896
- according to the dishes.
- Oh, yes.

501
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:33,363
Now, Lee Teuk and Shin Dong,

502
00:20:33,363 --> 00:20:34,463
please swap seats.

503
00:20:34,463 --> 00:20:35,696
- Huh?
- Like this?

504
00:20:35,696 --> 00:20:37,314
Oh, like this?

505
00:20:37,314 --> 00:20:39,382
- Oh, we're in trouble.
- Wait, wait a second.

506
00:20:39,382 --> 00:20:40,916
[Lee Teuk, Johnny, Ji Sung]
Oh, we're in trouble. Oh, Johnny…!

507
00:20:40,916 --> 00:20:43,063
[Don't come this way, Lee Teuk]
Lee Teuk!

508
00:20:43,063 --> 00:20:44,796
What? What trouble!

509
00:20:44,796 --> 00:20:46,163
[Frantic waving x127]
Lee Teuk, not this side!

510
00:20:46,163 --> 00:20:47,296
Hey, why are we in trouble?

511
00:20:47,296 --> 00:20:48,963
How can you give me duds?

512
00:20:48,963 --> 00:20:50,963
[Sudden jump]
Duds? What do you mean by "duds," Shin Dong?

513
00:20:50,963 --> 00:20:52,963
[I have no faith in these two]
What am I supposed to do with two duds?

514
00:20:52,963 --> 00:20:56,797
[His honest truth]
I honestly just wanted to send Ji Sung over.

515
00:20:56,797 --> 00:20:58,687
[A mission where being slim works against you]
I had a feeling, Johnny.

516
00:20:58,687 --> 00:21:00,163
Johnny, I really did.

517
00:21:00,163 --> 00:21:02,063
Johnny looks like he eats a lot, though.

518
00:21:02,063 --> 00:21:03,572
[Eats enough to maintain his energy]
I eat just enough…

519
00:21:03,572 --> 00:21:05,096
- Like what I see…
- I think he eats little.

520
00:21:05,096 --> 00:21:06,129
You don't like
leaving food behind, right?

521
00:21:06,129 --> 00:21:07,469
- Yeah, I hate leaving food.
- I really don't like it.

522
00:21:07,469 --> 00:21:08,556
[Hamster tries his best to impress]
I'm in my prime these days.

523
00:21:08,556 --> 00:21:09,596
You're in your prime? We're good.

524
00:21:09,596 --> 00:21:11,830
But the mission might
not be to eat everything.

525
00:21:11,830 --> 00:21:12,948
You have to finish everything.

526
00:21:12,948 --> 00:21:14,729
[Must eat all the food
to move to the next restaurant]

527
00:21:14,729 --> 00:21:15,930
I didn't understand the rules.

528
00:21:15,930 --> 00:21:18,220
- I eat super fast.
- I can finish a burger under a minute.

529
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:19,630
I can eat two hamburgers.

530
00:21:19,630 --> 00:21:21,897
[The person with the biggest disadvantage]
Oh, that's why they paired me up with DAWN!

531
00:21:21,897 --> 00:21:23,063
I surprisingly eat well!

532
00:21:23,063 --> 00:21:25,296
[Laughs]
Shin Dong, I really, probably…

533
00:21:25,296 --> 00:21:28,288
If you eat as much as I do? You'll die…

534
00:21:30,267 --> 00:21:32,325
Everyone's so nice, so…

535
00:21:32,325 --> 00:21:34,060
[Pure soul]
"The member lineup doesn't matter."

536
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:36,418
That was the first thought I had.

537
00:21:36,418 --> 00:21:38,296
Whoaaaaa!

538
00:21:38,296 --> 00:21:40,163
[The hamster jumps
in panic as a bug flies by]

539
00:21:40,163 --> 00:21:41,730
[That's not a bug]
It's just dust.

540
00:21:41,730 --> 00:21:42,730
Legendary.

541
00:21:42,730 --> 00:21:43,897
[Awkward hamster moment]

542
00:21:43,897 --> 00:21:47,030
It was just dust…
I thought it was a bug…Wow.

543
00:21:47,030 --> 00:21:48,919
[Kinda embarrassed
now that he thinks about it]

544
00:21:48,919 --> 00:21:51,583
I wasn't happy with it.

545
00:21:51,583 --> 00:21:56,026
It kind of felt like I had
two fragile kids stuck next to me.

546
00:21:56,026 --> 00:21:59,228
We'll reveal the keyword
for the first appetizer restaurant.

547
00:21:59,228 --> 00:22:00,629
[Revealing the keyword
for the first "Appetizer" restaurant]

548
00:22:00,629 --> 00:22:03,230
Once each team selects,
we'll mark it on the map for you.

549
00:22:03,230 --> 00:22:04,830
[After choosing,
the locations will be revealed on a map]

550
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:08,038
Now, the first keyword for
the appetizer restaurant is…

551
00:22:08,038 --> 00:22:09,172
A.

552
00:22:09,172 --> 00:22:12,307
[A = A flavorful national dish]
A flavorful national dish.

553
00:22:12,307 --> 00:22:14,277
- F.N.D!
- A flavorful national dish!

554
00:22:14,277 --> 00:22:15,879
F.N.D!

555
00:22:15,879 --> 00:22:16,947
B.

556
00:22:16,947 --> 00:22:18,589
- Healthy soul food.
- H.S!

557
00:22:18,589 --> 00:22:20,983
[B = Healthy soul food]
Healthy soul food.

558
00:22:20,983 --> 00:22:21,863
[Exchanging glances]

559
00:22:21,863 --> 00:22:22,865
Isn't it "A"?

560
00:22:22,865 --> 00:22:24,620
- Definitely!
- Definitely "A".

561
00:22:24,620 --> 00:22:25,487
[Both teams quickly lean towards A]
That side will pick "A" too.

562
00:22:25,487 --> 00:22:26,496
It's totally like spicy stir-fried pork.

563
00:22:26,496 --> 00:22:27,696
"B," "B."

564
00:22:27,696 --> 00:22:28,863
[Eyes full of confidence]
Why, Shin Dong?

565
00:22:28,863 --> 00:22:30,119
You wanna eat fast, right?

566
00:22:30,119 --> 00:22:32,829
Something healthy means smaller portions.

567
00:22:32,829 --> 00:22:34,898
[Team meeting time]
Please discuss and choose.

568
00:22:34,898 --> 00:22:38,734
National dishes come in huge portions.

569
00:22:38,734 --> 00:22:39,930
- Oh, you're right.
- Yeah.

570
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:41,603
[Successfully convinced]
It has to be large since it's a national dish

571
00:22:41,603 --> 00:22:43,103
[Egypt's staple food is]
And, what's the national dish here?

572
00:22:43,103 --> 00:22:44,908
[Meat & bread, so bound to get full fast]
It's meat and bread.

573
00:22:44,908 --> 00:22:47,309
I'm Korean, so I picked the national dish.

574
00:22:47,309 --> 00:22:49,896
But it's not our national dish…?
It's this nation's.

575
00:22:49,896 --> 00:22:51,563
[Kim Yo Han (Korean)]
Right, we're in Egypt.

576
00:22:51,563 --> 00:22:53,383
[Currently Egyptian]
Then, going with healthy food…

577
00:22:53,383 --> 00:22:55,986
I had a bit of faith in Yo Han, but…

578
00:22:55,986 --> 00:22:58,488
He's kind of a goofball, too… So…

579
00:22:58,488 --> 00:23:00,130
This isn't gonna be easy either…

580
00:23:00,130 --> 00:23:02,190
That's what I was thinking.

581
00:23:02,190 --> 00:23:04,263
Honestly, in places like this,

582
00:23:04,263 --> 00:23:06,330
it's better to pick
something you're not craving.

583
00:23:06,330 --> 00:23:07,997
So, I'm going with
the one I'm not feeling.

584
00:23:07,997 --> 00:23:09,563
[Blind faith in the leader 1]
I trust your gut feeling.

585
00:23:09,563 --> 00:23:12,067
- Then, I'll also trust you.
- Then, just trust me for the first one.

586
00:23:12,067 --> 00:23:13,696
Trust me, and if I'm wrong…

587
00:23:13,696 --> 00:23:15,205
For the next one, I'll trust you guys.

588
00:23:15,205 --> 00:23:17,039
For games like this... honestly,

589
00:23:17,039 --> 00:23:19,374
you gotta eat fast
and move on quickly.

590
00:23:19,374 --> 00:23:20,976
So there are two strategies!

591
00:23:20,976 --> 00:23:22,945
[1. Go nearby]
First, go to the closest spot.

592
00:23:22,945 --> 00:23:25,296
[2. Go for smaller portions]
Second, choose the place with less food.

593
00:23:25,296 --> 00:23:26,330
But,

594
00:23:26,330 --> 00:23:28,011
[1. Not sure which spot is closest]
if you don't know the exact location,

595
00:23:28,011 --> 00:23:30,053
then when choosing between the two,

596
00:23:30,053 --> 00:23:33,189
you have to pick the one
that seems to have less food.

597
00:23:33,189 --> 00:23:36,537
[Meanwhile, Team Lee Teuk is deep in debate]
Look, healthy food could actually be pizza.

598
00:23:36,537 --> 00:23:37,820
- Pizza's fast.
- Right.

599
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:38,852
Pizza's fast.

600
00:23:38,852 --> 00:23:41,897
But "healthy" sounds fancy,
so it might be served slowly.

601
00:23:41,897 --> 00:23:44,252
[Team Lee Teuk's logic #2]
But, in a way,

602
00:23:44,252 --> 00:23:46,129
[The overall location matters more]
The first choice is based on luck,

603
00:23:46,129 --> 00:23:47,596
because we have no clue where to go.

604
00:23:47,596 --> 00:23:48,897
We've made up our minds.

605
00:23:48,897 --> 00:23:50,407
- Should we say it first, then?
- Hold on, hold on.

606
00:23:50,407 --> 00:23:52,140
What do we do now?

607
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:55,143
But honestly speaking,
let's just choose romance…

608
00:23:55,143 --> 00:23:56,278
[Romance accepted]
That's really thrilling.

609
00:23:56,278 --> 00:23:58,223
And, even if it's just one meal!

610
00:23:58,223 --> 00:23:59,696
- Let's enjoy it!
- Enjoy it!

611
00:23:59,696 --> 00:24:00,763
If you enjoy your food,
then it's what?

612
00:24:00,763 --> 00:24:03,620
[Suddenly, enjoying food means zero calories]
It's zero calories.

613
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:05,709
For the first one,
we have to go for the shortest distance.

614
00:24:05,709 --> 00:24:09,359
Since the goal is to win the game,

615
00:24:09,359 --> 00:24:14,426
we were hoping the restaurants we picked
would all be close to each other…

616
00:24:14,426 --> 00:24:15,464
I think we were

617
00:24:15,464 --> 00:24:18,101
[Chasing romance while holding onto hope]
half excited and half nervous.

618
00:24:18,101 --> 00:24:20,036
[Team Lee Teuk chooses first]
We're here in Egypt, right?

619
00:24:20,036 --> 00:24:22,672
So we're gonna try
the national dish of Egypt.

620
00:24:22,672 --> 00:24:24,096
Two, three!

621
00:24:24,096 --> 00:24:26,042
"A"!

622
00:24:26,042 --> 00:24:27,909
Hey, you have to do it with me…

623
00:24:27,909 --> 00:24:29,311
You didn't even tell them to.

624
00:24:29,311 --> 00:24:31,264
[Unfair]
Like, you have to go with your gut!

625
00:24:31,264 --> 00:24:34,150
We'll go with the national dish of Egypt.

626
00:24:34,150 --> 00:24:36,130
[Trying again]
One, two, three!

627
00:24:36,130 --> 00:24:38,430
"A"!

628
00:24:38,430 --> 00:24:39,897
[Then, what will Team Shin Dong pick?]
Now, Team Shin Dong.

629
00:24:39,897 --> 00:24:41,324
For us,

630
00:24:41,324 --> 00:24:43,493
we sort of want to eat something light

631
00:24:43,493 --> 00:24:45,362
- for the first dish.
- Right, right.

632
00:24:45,362 --> 00:24:49,132
And it seems that the word
"healthy" stood out for us.

633
00:24:49,132 --> 00:24:50,329
So we made our choice.

634
00:24:50,329 --> 00:24:51,887
Our team picks…!

635
00:24:51,887 --> 00:24:53,956
[Team Shin Dong picks B: Healthy soul food]
"B"!

636
00:24:54,703 --> 00:24:56,763
[Revealing the first appetizer restaurant]
We'll reveal the locations of each restaurant.

637
00:24:56,763 --> 00:24:58,507
This is what's important.

638
00:24:58,507 --> 00:25:00,563
Let's take a look!

639
00:25:00,563 --> 00:25:02,210
- Oh!
- It doesn't matter.

640
00:25:02,210 --> 00:25:04,046
- I'm trusting Johnny on this.
- It's literally right next door.

641
00:25:04,046 --> 00:25:05,663
Oh, okay, okay.

642
00:25:05,663 --> 00:25:08,897
[A. A flavorful national dish]
[B. Healthy soul food]

643
00:25:08,897 --> 00:25:09,930
Oh, then this spot would be bad.

644
00:25:09,930 --> 00:25:11,697
[The problematic spots]
On both sides.

645
00:25:11,697 --> 00:25:14,730
- They gave us the ones in the middle on purpose.
- At least, we'll get there a little faster.

646
00:25:14,730 --> 00:25:16,196
Before you head out…!

647
00:25:16,196 --> 00:25:18,196
It'd be a shame to just end it here,
so we prepared a mini-game!

648
00:25:18,196 --> 00:25:19,105
- Okay.
- Alright.

649
00:25:19,105 --> 00:25:20,196
Is it to depart first?

650
00:25:20,196 --> 00:25:21,563
Or to pick our car?

651
00:25:21,563 --> 00:25:23,063
[The most important thing in a racing game]
When you're in a racing game,

652
00:25:23,063 --> 00:25:24,596
what matters most
to beat your opponent?

653
00:25:24,596 --> 00:25:25,296
- Items.
- Items.

654
00:25:25,296 --> 00:25:26,462
Banana peels.

655
00:25:26,462 --> 00:25:27,596
We'll play a game to get items!

656
00:25:27,596 --> 00:25:28,963
[A game to acquire special items]
Oh!

657
00:25:28,963 --> 00:25:30,540
Oh, there's something like this?

658
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:32,207
If it's an item, is it like a digestive aid?

659
00:25:32,207 --> 00:25:34,163
[Wild guess]
Or, like, a 5-minute wait in the car?

660
00:25:34,163 --> 00:25:35,396
Oh, could it be something like that?

661
00:25:35,396 --> 00:25:36,886
That would be so funny.

662
00:25:36,886 --> 00:25:38,448
[Lose one serving of our food?]
Or maybe lose one serving.

663
00:25:38,448 --> 00:25:39,530
[Add a serving to the other team!]
Or like add another serving.

664
00:25:39,530 --> 00:25:41,149
Add a serving to the other team.

665
00:25:41,149 --> 00:25:42,330
[Getting a crazy look in his eyes for some reason]
While you're eating, "What's this?"

666
00:25:42,330 --> 00:25:43,687
"The other team ordered it for you."

667
00:25:43,687 --> 00:25:45,755
"They've used an item."

668
00:25:45,755 --> 00:25:48,330
We'll begin the mini-game to acquire items.

669
00:25:48,330 --> 00:25:52,429
It's titled: "The Guardian of the Pyramid".

670
00:25:52,429 --> 00:25:53,897
You're going for a Sphinx vibe.

671
00:25:53,897 --> 00:25:56,963
You will all become the Sphinx yourselves

672
00:25:56,963 --> 00:25:59,529
and guard the pyramid.

673
00:25:59,529 --> 00:26:01,238
- Guard what?
- No way…

674
00:26:01,238 --> 00:26:03,674
Is it like standing
in front of it for as long as possible?

675
00:26:03,674 --> 00:26:07,363
From each team, one person will play.

676
00:26:07,363 --> 00:26:08,730
And like the Sphinx,

677
00:26:08,730 --> 00:26:11,953
the person who holds
a plank the longest…

678
00:26:12,630 --> 00:26:15,730
[Seven Wonders of the World]
[The pyramids]

679
00:26:15,730 --> 00:26:19,256
[The Sphinx, the guardian who watches in front]

680
00:26:19,256 --> 00:26:22,588
[Embody the Sphinx
and outlast your opponent!]

681
00:26:24,463 --> 00:26:27,430
[A plank in this heat?]
[Variety shows are tough these days...]

682
00:26:27,430 --> 00:26:29,530
It's 34 degrees Celsius here...

683
00:26:30,300 --> 00:26:32,163
Oh, this is the absolute worst for me.

684
00:26:32,163 --> 00:26:33,597
[Both teams wrestle with worry and confidence]
This is good. We're in a good spot.

685
00:26:33,597 --> 00:26:35,871
- It's not bad at all.
- Not bad at all. It's so great.

686
00:26:35,871 --> 00:26:37,015
Should we explain the items now?

687
00:26:37,015 --> 00:26:38,848
[What items will they get?]
Or later…

688
00:26:38,848 --> 00:26:41,042
Just give us a quick teaser.

689
00:26:41,042 --> 00:26:42,512
[Curious]
I gotta say

690
00:26:42,512 --> 00:26:44,763
I was impressed
by Lee Teuk's intuition earlier.

691
00:26:44,763 --> 00:26:45,996
It's one of the things he mentioned.

692
00:26:45,996 --> 00:26:47,264
- It is?
- Oh, really?

693
00:26:47,264 --> 00:26:50,755
The first item is
"The gentleman over there sent it".

694
00:26:52,543 --> 00:26:55,363
[First item]
[The gentleman over there sent it]

695
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:57,896
[While each person is eating a serving]

696
00:26:57,896 --> 00:27:00,828
[An extra serving will be
added when the item is used]

697
00:27:00,828 --> 00:27:03,166
We need to get that item,
no matter what.

698
00:27:03,166 --> 00:27:04,529
- I might curse while eating.
- I know, right?

699
00:27:04,529 --> 00:27:05,663
[Already worried]

700
00:27:05,663 --> 00:27:06,796
The second item is

701
00:27:06,796 --> 00:27:09,397
[Second item]
"One hand's just for support".

702
00:27:09,397 --> 00:27:11,563
- This one is…
- Is it eating with one hand?

703
00:27:11,563 --> 00:27:14,196
[Second item]
[One hand's just for support]

704
00:27:14,196 --> 00:27:17,196
[If the item is used during a meal]

705
00:27:17,196 --> 00:27:20,228
[You must eat with your hands
tied together like a three-legged race]

706
00:27:20,650 --> 00:27:23,220
That item is seriously the worst

707
00:27:23,220 --> 00:27:24,729
[Already uncomfortable just hearing it]
That's gonna be so uncomfortable.

708
00:27:24,729 --> 00:27:26,229
Let me introduce the third item.

709
00:27:26,229 --> 00:27:27,863
Played here in Egypt,

710
00:27:27,863 --> 00:27:30,196
[Third item]
a traditional coin game.

711
00:27:30,196 --> 00:27:31,363
[Is it the coin I know?]
Coin?

712
00:27:31,363 --> 00:27:33,230
- Not that coin.
