So, like, I'm confident against Lee Teuk.

948
00:35:57,430 --> 00:35:59,397
When it comes to DAWN,

949
00:35:59,397 --> 00:36:01,496
we all have this image in mind.

950
00:36:01,496 --> 00:36:02,672
Weakling.

951
00:36:02,672 --> 00:36:03,807
Toothpick.

952
00:36:03,807 --> 00:36:04,959
Chopstick.

953
00:36:04,959 --> 00:36:05,996
Thorn.

954
00:36:05,996 --> 00:36:07,163
Anchovy.

955
00:36:07,163 --> 00:36:10,463
I got the feeling
that I could beat him.

956
00:36:12,282 --> 00:36:13,683
Oh, wait, wait!

957
00:36:13,683 --> 00:36:15,496
[The weakling-thorn-anchovy
was waiting nearby]

958
00:36:15,496 --> 00:36:16,784
This is great.

959
00:36:16,784 --> 00:36:18,330
[Round 3: Battle of the prideful anchovies]
When you hear the whistle,

960
00:36:18,330 --> 00:36:20,723
you must raise your knees.

961
00:36:20,723 --> 00:36:23,520
[Which anchovy will win?]

962
00:36:24,792 --> 00:36:26,475
Lee Teuk, your hips are a bit high.

963
00:36:26,475 --> 00:36:27,731
Yeah, that's right.

964
00:36:27,731 --> 00:36:28,798
[Feedback applied immediately]
Lee Teuk.

965
00:36:28,798 --> 00:36:29,874
Huh? DAWN's hips are higher.

966
00:36:29,874 --> 00:36:31,268
- They're similar right now.
- No, his are higher.

967
00:36:31,268 --> 00:36:32,692
[A subtle hip-height standoff]
No, it's really similar.

968
00:36:32,692 --> 00:36:33,837
[Subtly]
DAWN, you don't have to do that.

969
00:36:33,837 --> 00:36:35,505
[Sincerely fine-tuning hip height]
Lee Teuk's hips are higher right now.

970
00:36:35,505 --> 00:36:36,373
Oh, Lee Teuk...!

971
00:36:36,373 --> 00:36:38,478
- Your hips were the highest!
- Right??

972
00:36:38,478 --> 00:36:39,606
[Awkward]
Yeah, I apologize.

973
00:36:39,606 --> 00:36:41,450
I shouldn't be calling anyone out.

974
00:36:50,428 --> 00:36:51,996
[1 minute elapsed]
1 minute has passed.

975
00:36:51,996 --> 00:36:53,030
Wow, they're being serious.

976
00:36:53,030 --> 00:36:54,230
They're serious.
Their expressions right now…

977
00:36:54,230 --> 00:36:55,289
Both of them are serious.

978
00:36:55,289 --> 00:36:57,831
[It's a battle of the anchovies,
but Round 3 is carrying on smoothly]

979
00:36:58,361 --> 00:37:00,994
Lee Teuk, you put
a ton of insoles in your shoes.

980
00:37:01,396 --> 00:37:03,997
[Humiliation]

981
00:37:03,997 --> 00:37:06,503
[Protect our brother]
They are really visible.

982
00:37:06,503 --> 00:37:11,061
[Johnny protects Lee Teuk's pride]
That's actually a phone.

983
00:37:11,596 --> 00:37:13,915
[With the top of
their heads even turning red]

984
00:37:17,896 --> 00:37:19,563
[They break the dreaded 2-minute mark]

985
00:37:19,563 --> 00:37:21,481
[2 minutes elapsed]
Okay, 2 minutes have passed.

986
00:37:21,481 --> 00:37:23,149
They'll slowly start feeling it now.

987
00:37:23,149 --> 00:37:25,455
Yeah, it hits hard right after 2 minutes.

988
00:37:25,455 --> 00:37:27,089
Lee Teuk's really good at this.

989
00:37:27,089 --> 00:37:28,111
But they're both really good.

990
00:37:28,111 --> 00:37:30,106
- There's no wobbling.
- Seriously, no wobble.

991
00:37:30,106 --> 00:37:32,329
[Meanwhile]
Lee Teuk is really not shaking at all.

992
00:37:32,329 --> 00:37:34,258
[I'll show you that even anchovies are strong]
I'll prove skinny guys can be strong too.

993
00:37:34,258 --> 00:37:36,316
Skinny sticks do burn well.

994
00:37:36,316 --> 00:37:37,539
[Those two]
I think they're doing the best at this.

995
00:37:37,539 --> 00:37:39,296
[Surprise main event: Lee Teuk VS DAWN]
- They're so chill. - They're the best at this.

996
00:37:39,296 --> 00:37:41,525
So you need to be light for this.

997
00:37:43,039 --> 00:37:44,307
- A little bit…
- It's coming, it's coming.

998
00:37:44,307 --> 00:37:45,602
Oh, Lee Teuk!

999
00:37:45,602 --> 00:37:46,664
It's here, it's here.

1000
00:37:46,664 --> 00:37:48,430
Lee Teuk's basically Cardi B right now.

1001
00:38:02,058 --> 00:38:03,260
[3 minutes elapsed]
3 minutes have passed.

1002
00:38:03,260 --> 00:38:05,362
Wow, they're really good.

1003
00:38:05,362 --> 00:38:08,298
[How did they hold on for 3 minutes?]
Wow, without even saying a word…!

1004
00:38:08,298 --> 00:38:09,472
Wow, they're both
really good at this.

1005
00:38:09,472 --> 00:38:10,454
It's here, it's here, it's here!

1006
00:38:10,454 --> 00:38:12,035
DAWN, you just need
to hold on a little longer!

1007
00:38:12,035 --> 00:38:13,103
- DAWN, you can win.
- For real.

1008
00:38:13,103 --> 00:38:14,263
[Both teams are hitting their limit]
He's feeling it, he's feeling it.

1009
00:38:14,263 --> 00:38:15,832
Lee Teuk's almost 50 soon.

1010
00:38:15,832 --> 00:38:17,939
You're gonna lose
to a 50-year-old?!

1011
00:38:17,939 --> 00:38:19,384
[Technically, he's 44 years old]
I'm 44.

1012
00:38:19,384 --> 00:38:21,978
- DAWN! This is the only thing you can do well!
- You, youngster!

1013
00:38:21,978 --> 00:38:23,000
You, youngster!

1014
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:25,179
[Get it together]
If you lose here, you'll be a pauper forever.

1015
00:38:25,179 --> 00:38:27,468
You're trying to beat an old guy?

1016
00:38:27,468 --> 00:38:30,533
[Proving age is but a number, while trembling]
Hey kid, just take it easy.

1017
00:38:30,533 --> 00:38:31,530
Whatever you do…

1018
00:38:31,530 --> 00:38:33,667
[No answer]
[Anchovy DAWN's grind continues]

1019
00:38:33,667 --> 00:38:35,825
It was totally unexpected.

1020
00:38:35,825 --> 00:38:38,562
Rather than an anchovy,

1021
00:38:38,562 --> 00:38:41,230
[Acknowledging his eel power]
he felt more like an eel.

1022
00:38:41,230 --> 00:38:42,930
He's got serious strength.

1023
00:38:42,930 --> 00:38:44,367
[Respect from one anchovy to another]
He's one tough guy.

1024
00:38:44,367 --> 00:38:46,029
I was really surprised.

1025
00:38:54,730 --> 00:38:56,330
They're both really good.

1026
00:38:56,330 --> 00:38:57,796
I think they're gonna hit 4 minutes.

1027
00:38:57,796 --> 00:38:59,830
[4 minutes elapsed]
4 minutes have passed.

1028
00:38:59,830 --> 00:39:01,284
They're gonna hit 5 minutes.

1029
00:39:01,284 --> 00:39:02,942
[Hang in there a bit longer]
DAWN's really done.

1030
00:39:02,942 --> 00:39:04,754
- He's gone.
- Yeah, it's over.

1031
00:39:04,754 --> 00:39:05,830
[Side glance]
He's shaking a lot.

1032
00:39:05,830 --> 00:39:06,823
He dropped a lot.

1033
00:39:06,823 --> 00:39:08,758
[No way]
No, DAWN will continue like this

1034
00:39:08,758 --> 00:39:10,594
for like 10 minutes.

1035
00:39:10,594 --> 00:39:12,295
[Eel DAWN fights to hold on]
Oh, but…!

1036
00:39:12,295 --> 00:39:14,024
Your core! Your core!
Hold out with your core!

1037
00:39:14,024 --> 00:39:15,997
- That's right! DAWN, just a bit more!
- Hold out with your core.

1038
00:39:15,997 --> 00:39:17,874
Just hang in there a little longer.

1039
00:39:17,874 --> 00:39:20,641
[Who will win Round 3?]

1040
00:39:24,796 --> 00:39:26,463
Wow!

1041
00:39:27,296 --> 00:39:28,629
[Wobble]

1042
00:39:28,629 --> 00:39:30,296
- No!
- No, DAWN!

1043
00:39:30,296 --> 00:39:32,029
Can I do something with this?

1044
00:39:32,029 --> 00:39:34,530
[Use this at least]
DAWN, I'm sorry, but just a little more!

1045
00:39:37,163 --> 00:39:39,990
Go down.

1046
00:39:39,990 --> 00:39:42,290
DAWN, I'm sorry.
I'm really sorry about this.

1047
00:39:42,290 --> 00:39:43,326
DAWN, just a little longer.

1048
00:39:43,326 --> 00:39:44,779
[Shin Dong, I can't do it]

1049
00:39:47,364 --> 00:39:48,861
[Recorded 4 minutes and 30 seconds]

1050
00:39:48,861 --> 00:39:51,701
[Round 3 winner: Lee Teuk]
Lee Teuk!

1051
00:39:51,701 --> 00:39:52,867
Oh, Lee Teuk!

1052
00:39:52,867 --> 00:39:55,173
[This is what old-man strength looks like]

1053
00:39:55,672 --> 00:39:58,098
[A loss but an epic match]
It's all good, it's all good.

1054
00:39:58,098 --> 00:40:01,373
[So close]
We can do this well. It's fine, it's fine.

1055
00:40:02,463 --> 00:40:03,914
Wow.

1056
00:40:03,914 --> 00:40:07,617
The record holder for the longest time
of the "ALL or NOTHING" plank challenge!

1057
00:40:07,617 --> 00:40:09,386
- Yes.
- Lee Teuk!

1058
00:40:09,386 --> 00:40:10,754
[Traditional coin game]
Thank you.

1059
00:40:10,754 --> 00:40:13,730
[Team Lee Teuk grabs the final item]
The oldest person has the longest plank record.

1060
00:40:13,730 --> 00:40:14,830
He must work out pretty regularly…

1061
00:40:14,830 --> 00:40:16,796
- He really does.
- Right?

1062
00:40:16,796 --> 00:40:18,163
[Team Shin Dong starts with only 1 item]
Otherwise, there's no way he could do that

1063
00:40:18,163 --> 00:40:20,129
- Seriously impressive.
- Congratulations.

1064
00:40:20,129 --> 00:40:21,773
You're reserved to be paupers.

1065
00:40:21,773 --> 00:40:23,630
- Us?
- Yes.

1066
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:26,228
[Trying to stay calm]
Just look at us. Who looks more like a pauper?

1067
00:40:26,228 --> 00:40:28,538
- Shin Dong, you're sweating buckets.
- Do I look too much like a pauper?

1068
00:40:28,538 --> 00:40:30,040
[You look the most like a pauper]
You look like a pauper.

1069
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:31,474
Yes.

1070
00:40:31,474 --> 00:40:33,343
I think I'm gonna
be sore tomorrow.

1071
00:40:33,343 --> 00:40:35,845
I'm already sore…

1072
00:40:35,845 --> 00:40:37,563
[While clutching their sore abs...]
DAWN, doesn't it hurt here?

1073
00:40:37,563 --> 00:40:39,530
- It's here for me.
- Oh, it hurts there?

1074
00:40:39,930 --> 00:40:44,097
[Each team heads
to their assigned restaurant!]

1075
00:40:44,097 --> 00:40:45,983
[Feeling anxious]
We gotta get there faster than the other team...

1076
00:40:45,983 --> 00:40:48,058
But I suddenly

1077
00:40:48,058 --> 00:40:49,659
lost my confidence…

1078
00:40:49,659 --> 00:40:51,985
[Wait, what...]
We're here because we trusted you, though.

1079
00:40:51,985 --> 00:40:53,830
[You told us to trust you earlier...]
You can't suddenly do this to us.

1080
00:40:53,830 --> 00:40:57,754
[Trying to backtrack]
I'm suddenly sleepy. So strange.

1081
00:40:57,754 --> 00:41:00,237
[Must-have requirement]
Still, you two eat well, right?

1082
00:41:00,237 --> 00:41:01,071
[Eats well]
I do eat well.

1083
00:41:01,071 --> 00:41:02,349
[Not picky]
I'm not picky at all.

1084
00:41:02,349 --> 00:41:03,540
DAWN, you really eat a lot, right…?

1085
00:41:03,540 --> 00:41:05,873
[Extremely suspicious]
I'm really pretty good.

1086
00:41:05,873 --> 00:41:07,812
As long as it's not that. Lamb!

1087
00:41:07,812 --> 00:41:08,945
Oh, so there's
something you can't eat.

1088
00:41:08,945 --> 00:41:10,545
- Tell us what you can't eat.
- Anything fishy.

1089
00:41:10,545 --> 00:41:13,306
But Yo Han, since you did sports growing up,
you must've eaten a lot of things.

1090
00:41:13,306 --> 00:41:15,896
Yeah, if I didn't eat,
I used to get hit.

1091
00:41:16,586 --> 00:41:19,344
[Baby Yo Han grew up especially tough]
It was like that when we grew up. We got hit.

1092
00:41:19,344 --> 00:41:22,684
[Time for a strategy]
Which do you prefer, seafood and meat?

1093
00:41:23,159 --> 00:41:24,892
- Seafood for me!
- If you had to choose…Oh, seafood!

1094
00:41:24,892 --> 00:41:25,962
I'm not really into seafood.

1095
00:41:25,962 --> 00:41:27,447
Oh, I love seafood!

1096
00:41:27,447 --> 00:41:28,496
What about you?

1097
00:41:28,496 --> 00:41:30,100
[What about Yo Han?]
Seafood or meat?

1098
00:41:30,100 --> 00:41:33,058
- I basically eat whatever's given to me…
- Oh, then, okay! For you,

1099
00:41:33,058 --> 00:41:34,404
[In charge of big servings]
you eat a lot of both.

1100
00:41:34,404 --> 00:41:35,870
[In charge of the meat]
I'll eat a lot of the meat.

1101
00:41:35,870 --> 00:41:37,031
- You eat a lot of seafood.
- I'll eat lots of seafood.

1102
00:41:37,031 --> 00:41:38,363
[Tasks divided in a flash]
Okay.

1103
00:41:38,363 --> 00:41:41,130
I roughly looked up
healthy soul food online.

1104
00:41:41,130 --> 00:41:42,463
What did you find?

1105
00:41:42,463 --> 00:41:43,480
Beans!

1106
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:45,279
Right? The beans here seem pretty famous.

1107
00:41:45,279 --> 00:41:46,449
- Lentils and stuff.
- Chickpeas.

1108
00:41:46,449 --> 00:41:48,049
[Just hearing it feels healthy]
Chickpeas came up a lot.

1109
00:41:48,049 --> 00:41:52,355
[Hmm...]
A soup made of…green leafy veggies…

1110
00:41:53,554 --> 00:41:55,197
Oh, I'm really good
at eating noodles.

1111
00:41:55,197 --> 00:41:56,596
Filajel...

1112
00:41:56,596 --> 00:41:58,292
Falafel?

1113
00:41:58,292 --> 00:41:59,363
Doesn't this seem healthy?

1114
00:41:59,363 --> 00:42:01,562
[Dubai Chewy Chocolate style]
A vegan menu.

1115
00:42:01,562 --> 00:42:02,396
Whatever it is,

1116
00:42:02,396 --> 00:42:04,832
[Mind says health; heart says national dish.]
we just have to eat it.

1117
00:42:04,832 --> 00:42:06,530
That's right.

1118
00:42:06,530 --> 00:42:08,596
I'm extremely hungry right now.

1119
00:42:08,596 --> 00:42:10,129
[Planning to win on hunger alone]

1120
00:42:10,129 --> 00:42:12,363
Our card is...

1121
00:42:12,363 --> 00:42:14,477
- just the hand-tying one, right?
- Yeah.

1122
00:42:14,477 --> 00:42:16,825
[Another meeting agenda: Attack items]
We gotta have a plan for this.

1123
00:42:16,825 --> 00:42:18,879
[Using attack items]
Rather than using them right away,

1124
00:42:18,879 --> 00:42:20,596
I think it's better
to save it for the end.

1125
00:42:20,596 --> 00:42:21,828
During Round 3.

1126
00:42:21,828 --> 00:42:24,254
[Agreeing]
- Round 3? - Because

1127
00:42:24,254 --> 00:42:26,378
at first, they're starving,
so they'll eat like crazy.

1128
00:42:26,378 --> 00:42:28,529
Like, they'll bring the food
close to their mouths to eat faster.

1129
00:42:28,529 --> 00:42:29,550
But later,

1130
00:42:29,550 --> 00:42:31,695
[Planning to attack when they're full]
in round 3, they'll be stuffed.

1131
00:42:31,695 --> 00:42:34,158
Or, since seafood

1132
00:42:34,158 --> 00:42:36,095
is hard to eat with a fork…

1133
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:37,029
- Seafood is a good idea, Shin Dong!
- Right?

1134
00:42:37,029 --> 00:42:38,765
- Oh, seafood!
- You have to peel with your hands.

1135
00:42:38,765 --> 00:42:40,265
- You have to peel it!
- Right, right!

1136
00:42:40,265 --> 00:42:41,396
[Impressed]
Wow, Shin Dong, you're super strategic.

1137
00:42:41,396 --> 00:42:42,670
So, at that point…

1138
00:42:42,670 --> 00:42:44,174
[Smart]
Either during seafood or Round 3.

1139
00:42:44,174 --> 00:42:48,497
First, Shin Dong is seriously a strategist.

1140
00:42:48,497 --> 00:42:51,931
Shin Dong totally feels
like the brain of the team.

1141
00:42:51,931 --> 00:42:54,463
[Feeling safe with Strategist Shin Dong]
So, I was like, "Oh? This is so good."

1142
00:42:54,463 --> 00:42:55,886
[Deep in thought...]

1143
00:42:55,886 --> 00:42:58,283
From what I think,
as soon as it starts,

1144
00:42:58,283 --> 00:43:00,490
don't you think
they'll use the one-serving item?

1145
00:43:00,490 --> 00:43:01,890
[Helpless...]

1146
00:43:01,890 --> 00:43:04,699
[Preparing to eat 4 servings from the start]
We gotta just assume we're eating 4 servings.

1147
00:43:05,095 --> 00:43:08,329
But would they use
an item for healthy soul food?

1148
00:43:08,329 --> 00:43:09,566
[Is that right?]
Perhaps for larger portions?

1149
00:43:09,566 --> 00:43:11,793
I feel they'll use it
when we eat meat or something like that.

1150
00:43:11,793 --> 00:43:13,263
No, from what I see,

1151
00:43:13,263 --> 00:43:15,769
that team has no strategists.

1152
00:43:15,769 --> 00:43:17,386
All three of them
are just muscle power.

1153
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:19,175
[While Team Shin Dong is
working hard on their strategy…]

1154
00:43:19,175 --> 00:43:21,044
Oh, right, we have to decide that.

1155
00:43:21,044 --> 00:43:23,277
After eating the first dish,
for the second dish…

1156
00:43:23,277 --> 00:43:25,396
We have to decide

1157
00:43:25,396 --> 00:43:27,284
if we're going with meat or fish.

1158
00:43:27,284 --> 00:43:28,696
[What?]
The order…

1159
00:43:28,696 --> 00:43:30,430
Isn't it already set?

1160
00:43:30,430 --> 00:43:32,856
- Like, which restaurant to go to…
- Oh, I didn't understand it.

1161
00:43:32,856 --> 00:43:33,924
[Reset]
So, it's decided?

1162
00:43:33,924 --> 00:43:35,292
[Still don't understand the rules]
You didn't know, right? Ji Sung?

1163
00:43:35,292 --> 00:43:36,783
[He's in the same boat]
I thought we had to decide.

1164
00:43:36,783 --> 00:43:37,894
- The order is fixed.
- Yeah.

1165
00:43:37,894 --> 00:43:41,097
- We have to decide what restaurant to go to.
- Right.

1166
00:43:41,097 --> 00:43:43,700
Aren't we deciding
if we're eating fish or meat?

1167
00:43:43,700 --> 00:43:46,670
[It's not that…]
There are two fish restaurants.

1168
00:43:46,670 --> 00:43:50,030
[Choose one of the two seafood spots,
or one of the two meat places]

1169
00:43:50,030 --> 00:43:51,041
That's right.

1170
00:43:51,041 --> 00:43:53,309
[You got it, right?]
Oh, okay! I get it now.

1171
00:43:53,309 --> 00:43:54,201
And right now,

1172
00:43:54,201 --> 00:43:55,645
[Team Shin Dong's attack item]
the one item we'll get

1173
00:43:55,645 --> 00:43:58,433
- is the hand-tying one.
- Yes.

1174
00:43:58,433 --> 00:43:59,649
I feel like they'll use it immediately…

1175
00:43:59,649 --> 00:44:01,874
It's actually better
if they use it for the start.

1176
00:44:01,874 --> 00:44:03,787
[If their hands are tied]
Like, if they use it when we're eating steak?

1177
00:44:03,787 --> 00:44:05,733
That'd be a disaster.

1178
00:44:05,733 --> 00:44:08,063
[The smartest of the bunch]
Because we have to cut it.

1179
