01:02:16,880 --> 01:02:18,344
When this show ends,

1654
01:02:18,344 --> 01:02:21,197
we'll either leave super close,
or feud-ridden.

1655
01:02:21,197 --> 01:02:22,863
It'll be one of the two.

1656
01:02:22,863 --> 01:02:24,530
Actually, Johnny…

1657
01:02:24,530 --> 01:02:25,697
If there's something
Ji Sung and I can't eat,

1658
01:02:25,697 --> 01:02:26,930
you have to eat it for us.

1659
01:02:26,930 --> 01:02:28,230
Because… Hear me out.

1660
01:02:28,230 --> 01:02:30,930
Ji Sung and I won our matches.

1661
01:02:30,930 --> 01:02:32,295
- But you lost yours.
- Oh!

1662
01:02:32,295 --> 01:02:33,630
But that kind of makes sense…!

1663
01:02:33,630 --> 01:02:35,048
[Right?!]
Yeah, it does, right?

1664
01:02:35,048 --> 01:02:38,198
[The team's lone strategist becomes the target]
We need our own set of rules.

1665
01:02:38,198 --> 01:02:39,323
Today,

1666
01:02:39,323 --> 01:02:41,471
- Today, we're gonna lose.
- No, no, no.

1667
01:02:41,471 --> 01:02:43,872
You have to do it for us.
You're our team's ace!

1668
01:02:43,872 --> 01:02:46,215
An ace who loses?

1669
01:02:47,177 --> 01:02:51,079
But if we become paupers,
exactly how poor are we gonna be?

1670
01:02:51,079 --> 01:02:52,146
Like, super poor?!

1671
01:02:52,146 --> 01:02:54,009
[Extreme]
Like, no phones allowed…

1672
01:02:54,009 --> 01:02:55,297
They wouldn't
actually take our phones, right?

1673
01:02:55,297 --> 01:02:57,863
[Not that extreme]
We'll give you phones.

1674
01:02:57,863 --> 01:03:00,724
And then, the paupers
have to go to the king's house

1675
01:03:00,724 --> 01:03:02,893
and pay their respects, right?

1676
01:03:02,893 --> 01:03:04,463
[Wow, that's a great idea?]

1677
01:03:04,463 --> 01:03:05,663
- Pay their respects…
- Hey, don't say things like that.

1678
01:03:05,663 --> 01:03:08,030
[The staff wasn't even thinking about that…]
The production team didn't even consider that.

1679
01:03:08,030 --> 01:03:09,163
When you watch
dating reality shows,

1680
01:03:09,163 --> 01:03:12,930
some people never
even make it to paradise.

1681
01:03:12,930 --> 01:03:14,497
All-paupers.

1682
01:03:14,497 --> 01:03:16,163
- Pauper all the way.
- Pauper all the way.

1683
01:03:16,163 --> 01:03:17,696
But that could be better.

1684
01:03:17,696 --> 01:03:20,795
Going from prince to pauper
would be so brutal!

1685
01:03:20,795 --> 01:03:23,562
But if you keep living as a pauper,
you'll be like, "Oh, so this is how it is!"

1686
01:03:23,562 --> 01:03:25,532
Then, let's be paupers today.

1687
01:03:25,532 --> 01:03:27,396
[Startled]
No, no.

1688
01:03:28,118 --> 01:03:30,177
[The reliable big brother who goes back and forth]
Lee Teuk is so inconsistent!

1689
01:03:30,177 --> 01:03:31,944
Johnny.

1690
01:03:31,944 --> 01:03:33,657
Rather than that,
let's just keep winning.

1691
01:03:33,657 --> 01:03:36,508
[Real talk]
I don't think I can be a pauper…

1692
01:03:37,427 --> 01:03:39,360
But even if I become a pauper,
it would seem weird.

1693
01:03:39,360 --> 01:03:42,360
A chubby pauper is just strange.

1694
01:03:42,888 --> 01:03:45,902
[A well-fed pauper is odd to everyone]
Isn't a well-fed pauper kind of weird?

1695
01:03:45,902 --> 01:03:48,375
[Resolution]
I guess we have to be princes then.

1696
01:03:48,905 --> 01:03:49,973
We've gone a bit out now.

1697
01:03:49,973 --> 01:03:52,131
[Team Shin Dong slowly eases into the outskirts]
Yeah, we left the city quickly.

1698
01:03:52,131 --> 01:03:54,578
Wow! This place…!
It's got night market vibes!

1699
01:03:54,578 --> 01:03:55,603
[In awe]
Wow!

1700
01:03:55,603 --> 01:03:57,247
This place is amazing!

1701
01:03:57,247 --> 01:03:58,415
Wow!

1702
01:03:58,415 --> 01:03:59,916
[Endless rows of street shops
unfold outside the window]

1703
01:03:59,916 --> 01:04:01,151
This kinda reminds me of…

1704
01:04:01,151 --> 01:04:03,320
- Dongmyo style?
- Yeah.

1705
01:04:03,320 --> 01:04:05,799
- There's no end.
- Wow!

1706
01:04:05,799 --> 01:04:07,624
Wow, this is amazing.

1707
01:04:07,624 --> 01:04:08,758
Oh, they said it's a market.

1708
01:04:08,758 --> 01:04:09,629
Wow!!!

1709
01:04:09,629 --> 01:04:11,494
This place is seriously incredible!

1710
01:04:11,494 --> 01:04:13,060
[Amazed]
Wow!

1711
01:04:13,663 --> 01:04:16,365
Wow, it's really
densely populated here.

1712
01:04:16,365 --> 01:04:18,201
Cairo alone has
about 20 million people.

1713
01:04:18,201 --> 01:04:19,565
Really?

1714
01:04:19,565 --> 01:04:23,006
Then again, Egypt is like
10 times the size of Korea…

1715
01:04:23,396 --> 01:04:26,596
This must be a fabric market!
There are tons of fabrics.

1716
01:04:27,198 --> 01:04:31,769
[True to Egypt's fame for cotton,
the fabric market is bustling]

1717
01:04:35,163 --> 01:04:38,697
If we become princes, do we get to wear
traditional clothes and do this kind of thing?

1718
01:04:38,697 --> 01:04:40,896
I wanna try
wearing it at least once.

1719
01:04:41,296 --> 01:04:42,496
I think it'd be super comfy.

1720
01:04:42,496 --> 01:04:46,430
[That wish will come true one day]

1721
01:04:46,430 --> 01:04:48,665
[Heart flutter]

1722
01:04:48,665 --> 01:04:51,030
[This time, Lee Teuk makes a spy call]
Lee Teuk is calling, everyone.

1723
01:04:51,030 --> 01:04:52,630
They must've finished eating.

1724
01:04:52,630 --> 01:04:54,430
Yes, hello?

1725
01:04:54,430 --> 01:04:55,930
Did you enjoy your meal?

1726
01:04:55,930 --> 01:04:57,796
You just finished it now?!

1727
01:04:57,796 --> 01:04:59,096
We got like a giant bowl of food.

1728
01:04:59,096 --> 01:05:01,953
[LOL]

1729
01:05:02,546 --> 01:05:05,378
Shin Dong, you predicted correctly!

1730
01:05:05,378 --> 01:05:07,430
[I am Strategist Shin Dong]
I predicted it exactly.

1731
01:05:07,430 --> 01:05:10,263
Lee Teuk, what did you pick
for the second course?

1732
01:05:10,263 --> 01:05:12,596
[Shin Dong] Did you pick "A" or "B"?

1733
01:05:13,197 --> 01:05:14,296
Oh, they picked "A."

1734
01:05:14,296 --> 01:05:15,763
I still don't
understand that part.

1735
01:05:15,763 --> 01:05:17,527
Oh, you picked "A?"

1736
01:05:17,527 --> 01:05:19,029
Yeah, you picked "B," huh?

1737
01:05:19,029 --> 01:05:20,764
Yes, we picked "B."

1738
01:05:20,764 --> 01:05:22,328
[Lee Teuk]
Oh my...

1739
01:05:22,328 --> 01:05:24,996
[Testing the waters]
"A" seemed to be in a really far place.

1740
01:05:24,996 --> 01:05:27,904
[Not buying it]
"A" is actually closer.

1741
01:05:27,904 --> 01:05:30,835
No, "A" was really far away.

1742
01:05:30,835 --> 01:05:32,909
[Confident]
We're almost there already, though?

1743
01:05:32,909 --> 01:05:34,177
[Surprised]
Already?

1744
01:05:34,177 --> 01:05:35,312
You're right.

1745
01:05:35,312 --> 01:05:37,280
We just need to cross one bridge.

1746
01:05:37,280 --> 01:05:38,515
[Revealing true feelings]
Oh…We're in trouble.

1747
01:05:38,515 --> 01:05:39,812
Okay, Lee Teuk.

1748
01:05:39,812 --> 01:05:42,018
[The tables turn in an instant]
The tables turned immediately.

1749
01:05:42,018 --> 01:05:44,354
I heard it takes you
40 minutes to get there.

1750
01:05:44,354 --> 01:05:45,956
We finished our second course

1751
01:05:45,956 --> 01:05:48,181
[Bluffing]
and are headed to our third one.

1752
01:05:48,181 --> 01:05:49,226
Oh, really?

1753
01:05:49,226 --> 01:05:51,861
[An endless cycle of deception]
Our extra serving is headed your way soon.

1754
01:05:51,861 --> 01:05:54,596
Oh, yes, thank you so much.

1755
01:05:54,596 --> 01:05:56,866
Yes, sir.

1756
01:05:56,866 --> 01:05:58,501
Oh, we're in trouble…

1757
01:05:58,501 --> 01:05:59,970
Team Lee Teuk's spot is closer.

1758
01:05:59,970 --> 01:06:02,405
This is what I was worried about…

1759
01:06:02,405 --> 01:06:03,803
Should we use the item now?!

1760
01:06:03,803 --> 01:06:05,228
- No.
- Let's use it for Round 3.

1761
01:06:05,228 --> 01:06:07,173
We're going all the way to the right side now.

1762
01:06:07,173 --> 01:06:09,809
If we pick wrong next time
and end up all the way on the left…

1763
01:06:09,809 --> 01:06:10,962
We'll lose for sure.

1764
01:06:10,962 --> 01:06:12,649
[Guaranteed to be paupers]
That will be really…

1765
01:06:12,649 --> 01:06:15,915
We're reading each other's moves.

1766
01:06:15,915 --> 01:06:18,518
We totally know
each other inside out.

1767
01:06:18,518 --> 01:06:19,864
I feel like we're almost there.

1768
01:06:19,864 --> 01:06:21,996
Hey, we must be
going somewhere nice.

1769
01:06:21,996 --> 01:06:25,430
This place has
something like a Han River view.

1770
01:06:25,430 --> 01:06:27,563
Nile River view.

1771
01:06:28,230 --> 01:06:30,563
[Embracing thousands of years]
Wow, this place is stunning!

1772
01:06:30,563 --> 01:06:33,333
[A restaurant by the Nile River]

1773
01:06:36,840 --> 01:06:39,142
It has that Han River vibe
you mentioned earlier!

1774
01:06:39,142 --> 01:06:40,869
[Found the hint]
Yeah, total Han River vibes.

1775
01:06:40,869 --> 01:06:43,635
Oh! It might be
on the murals here.

1776
01:06:47,063 --> 01:06:49,596
[Egyptian murals displayed at the entrance]
The Egyptian murals are drawn here like this.

1777
01:06:49,596 --> 01:06:51,729
Since it's a seafood spot…

1778
01:06:53,130 --> 01:06:56,259
Assalamu alaikum!

1779
01:06:56,259 --> 01:06:58,551
Wow!!
The view is amazing!

1780
01:06:58,551 --> 01:07:00,084
The view is seriously so nice!

1781
01:07:01,295 --> 01:07:03,896
[Where your eyes and palate
are charmed at the same time]

1782
01:07:03,896 --> 01:07:05,163
This is nice.

1783
01:07:05,163 --> 01:07:06,863
Oh? It's just one! What a relief!

1784
01:07:06,863 --> 01:07:08,668
Hey, there's definitely lemon.

1785
01:07:08,668 --> 01:07:11,763
- Okay, shall we begin?
- We're jumping right in! Here we go!

1786
01:07:11,763 --> 01:07:14,581
- Open, open, open! Let's go!
- One, two, three!

1787
01:07:14,581 --> 01:07:16,248
- Oh!
- Okay, okay!

1788
01:07:18,030 --> 01:07:20,963
[A little luxury spread out on the table]

1789
01:07:22,185 --> 01:07:26,072
[Freshness that
embodies the deep blue Red Sea]

1790
01:07:29,463 --> 01:07:33,263
[Paired with fresh veggies and seasoning]

1791
01:07:33,263 --> 01:07:37,665
[Grilled over a strong fire]

1792
01:07:37,665 --> 01:07:38,896
[Grouper]

1793
01:07:38,896 --> 01:07:41,145
[Known as the "Beef of the Sea",
a grouper-family fish with firm, savory meat]

1794
01:07:42,764 --> 01:07:46,238
[Grouper / Just the right amount]

1795
01:07:46,238 --> 01:07:47,496
- This seriously looks good!
- It looks so good! It looks so good!

1796
01:07:47,496 --> 01:07:48,463
Okay!

1797
01:07:48,463 --> 01:07:49,696
First…!

1798
01:07:50,930 --> 01:07:54,163
[A quick check for bones]

1799
01:07:54,163 --> 01:07:55,986
[Taking it all in]
But like…this place is nice.

1800
01:07:55,986 --> 01:07:57,563
[High expectations]
This looks so delicious.

1801
01:07:57,563 --> 01:07:59,518
Ji Sung, here.

1802
01:07:59,518 --> 01:08:01,629
[The eldest takes care of the youngest first]
The meat, the meat.

1803
01:08:01,629 --> 01:08:03,130
Thank you.

1804
01:08:05,696 --> 01:08:07,096
How is it?

1805
01:08:07,096 --> 01:08:08,427
It's really good!

1806
01:08:08,427 --> 01:08:09,497
It's really good?

1807
01:08:09,497 --> 01:08:11,230
It kind of reminds me of
something I had in China.

1808
01:08:11,230 --> 01:08:13,563
It has a bit of a smoky flavor!

1809
01:08:13,563 --> 01:08:16,163
[Nom]
There are so many flavors.

1810
01:08:16,996 --> 01:08:18,630
Yeah, it's like…

1811
01:08:18,630 --> 01:08:21,963
Have you tried
pepper crab in Singapore before?

1812
01:08:21,963 --> 01:08:23,197
[Pepper crab]
Oh yeah, it's seriously yummy.

1813
01:08:23,197 --> 01:08:24,343
It has that kind of vibe.

1814
01:08:24,343 --> 01:08:25,945
[A crab dish with a mix of spices
and black pepper]

1815
01:08:30,383 --> 01:08:31,296
This is good.

1816
01:08:31,296 --> 01:08:33,414
- So good.
- So good. It's really good.

1817
01:08:33,414 --> 01:08:36,026
[Safe to say the food is good,
judging from how fast they're digging in]

1818
01:08:36,026 --> 01:08:38,962
So, this is what's
on the Egyptian murals.

1819
01:08:38,962 --> 01:08:40,697
We picked well for this one…!

1820
01:08:40,697 --> 01:08:42,705
[Peak satisfaction]
This is so good.

1821
01:08:42,705 --> 01:08:44,705
- I like the peppery part of it.
- Right?

1822
01:08:44,705 --> 01:08:45,902
The pepper taste is…

1823
01:08:45,902 --> 01:08:47,997
So you like pepper too?

1824
01:08:47,997 --> 01:08:50,030
I think it has
curry powder and turmeric.

1825
01:08:50,030 --> 01:08:51,964
- It does, right?
- Yeah.

1826
01:08:51,964 --> 01:08:54,630
Huh? Who…are you?!?!

1827
01:08:56,496 --> 01:08:58,458
[What's happening…?]

1828
01:08:59,755 --> 01:09:02,643
[A dark figure silently creeps in]

1829
01:09:03,679 --> 01:09:05,622
Oh, you scared me…!

1830
01:09:05,622 --> 01:09:07,815
[Bewildered eyes]

1831
01:09:08,696 --> 01:09:12,296
[And the suspicious item
in the suspicious person's hand]

1832
01:09:12,296 --> 01:09:13,196
[Please]

1833
01:09:13,196 --> 01:09:14,330
[Give me your hands]

1834
01:09:14,330 --> 01:09:16,373
[Attack item]
[Team Shin Dong used it…!]

1835
01:09:17,367 --> 01:09:18,666
What if they feed each other?

1836
01:09:18,666 --> 01:09:19,832
[Excited just imagining it]
Like, their hands are tied.

1837
01:09:19,832 --> 01:09:21,104
They'll purposely push it around,
like, "You eat it."

1838
01:09:21,104 --> 01:09:22,522
[Used an attack item at the right timing]
I think they'll drop it all.

1839
01:09:22,522 --> 01:09:23,740
Lee Teuk, you don't
have to tie your hands, right?

1840
01:09:23,740 --> 01:09:25,075
Since we're on this side?

1841
01:09:25,075 --> 01:09:27,467
[Why...?]
Am I getting tied too?

1842
01:09:27,467 --> 01:09:29,492
[Obviously]
Am I getting tied too?

1843
01:09:29,492 --> 01:09:31,477
[Oh...]
I somehow ended up in the middle.

1844
01:09:31,477 --> 01:09:33,049
[Bring it over]
Should we do it like this?

1845
01:09:33,049 --> 01:09:35,619
[They keep trying to start a conversation, but…]
Isn't this something we should decide?

1846
01:09:35,619 --> 01:09:37,596
Did you talk about
how to tie us together?

1847
01:09:37,596 --> 01:09:40,186
[Just doing it because it's work]
[The person in black is quite shy]

1848
01:09:40,186 --> 01:09:41,224
Ji Sung.

1849
01:09:41,224 --> 01:09:42,891
You just stay seated.

1850
01:09:43,688 --> 01:09:44,724
Ji Sung.

1851
01:09:44,724 --> 01:09:46,975
[The meal resumes
in a rather rude posture]

1852
01:09:46,975 --> 01:09:48,861
But Lee Teuk, don't you think
it's so romantic right now?

1853
01:09:48,861 --> 01:09:51,251
Our Ji Sung, open wide!

1854
01:09:51,630 --> 01:09:53,695
[The night deepens in Cairo]

1855
01:09:53,695 --> 01:09:55,430
[With the race getting an upgrade]

1856
01:09:55,430 --> 01:09:57,397
[The vibe changes 180 degrees?!]

1857
01:09:57,397 --> 01:09:58,158
Eat faster!

1858
01:09:58,158 --> 01:10:00,797
[If all they did so far was eat…]

1859
01:10:00,797 --> 01:10:02,298
[Get it together]
This is driving me crazy.

1860
01:10:02,298 --> 01:10:04,730
[The mind games will begin now]

1861
01:10:04,730 --> 01:10:06,099
[With rampant interference]
Lee Teuk, can you please wait for us?

1862
01:10:06,099 --> 01:10:07,530
We're gonna take a while.

1863
01:10:07,530 --> 01:10:08,630
[And growing suspicion]
I don't think I can trust them!

1864
01:10:08,630 --> 01:10:10,654
Hey, we told you
everything so honestly.

1865
01:10:10,654 --> 01:10:11,784
[The endless]
We're gonna use our item.

1866
01:10:11,784 --> 01:10:14,496
[The endless sabotage attempts]
Why are you sending so many missions?

1867
01:10:14,496 --> 01:10:16,588
[The pauper life inches closer]
Oh no, this is bad. Wait.

1868
01:10:16,588 --> 01:10:18,213
[Those who want to be princes]
We're in big trouble.

1869
01:10:18,213 --> 01:10:19,338
Let's go!

1870
01:10:19,338 --> 01:10:21,224
Compared to coming from here,
we're way faster.

1871
01:10:21,224 --> 01:10:23,363
- Right? Way faster, for sure.
- Go faster!

1872
01:10:24,134 --> 01:10:25,735
[However, never let your guard down]
Why is the traffic so bad?

1873
01:10:25,735 --> 01:10:26,960
Don't let your guard down.

1874
01:10:26,960 --> 01:10:28,318
[Until the very end, there's no way of knowing]
I'm nervous. Aren't you nervous?

1875
01:10:28,318 --> 01:10:30,419
I honestly thought we'd win.

1876
01:10:30,419 --> 01:10:33,554
[The results of this race of false hope!]
It keeps giving me hope until the end.

1877
01:10:33,554 --> 01:10:36,446
[For the paupers who lost the race]
This can't be real.

1878
01:10:36,446 --> 01:10:37,547
[The world's only desert suite…]

1879
01:10:37,547 --> 01:10:39,115
Are reality shows usually this hard?

1880
01:10:39,115 --> 01:10:43,383
[Who will be the winners of this fate?]

1881
01:10:43,383 --> 01:10:46,332
[And… "ALL or NOTHING" leaves Cairo]

1882
01:10:47,157 --> 01:10:48,225
Wow, this is amazing.

1883
01:10:48,225 --> 01:10:50,953
[What's the next destination?]
This is what travel's all about.

1884
01:10:51,764 --> 01:10:53,730
[Doubling the desire to win]

1885
01:10:53,730 --> 01:10:56,737
[A luxury cruise fit for a prince]
Oh, it's here!

1886
01:10:56,737 --> 01:10:58,196
Wow, this is so romantic!

1887
01:10:58,196 --> 01:11:02,806
[What's the next mission
that'll unfold in this romantic new city?]
